h('3. Exact address-color restriction')
p('<b>Proposition.</b> Let H_A be any finite address space and H_C=(C^3) tensor (C^3) tensor (C^3), carrying the same fundamental SU(3) action on each factor. Let P project onto the common kernel of the eight Q_a. If a density operator Omega satisfies Omega=(I_A tensor P) Omega (I_A tensor P), then P=|S><S| and Omega=sigma_A tensor |S><S| for a unique address density operator sigma_A.')
p('<b>Proof.</b> The two diagonal traceless generators require equal occupation of all three colors, leaving only the six permutations of rgb. For each pair of colors, the raising operator maps two permutations differing by their exchange to the same repeated-color output. Its vanishing forces opposite coefficients. These transposition relations connect all six permutations, fixing their coefficients up to an overall amplitude and permutation parity. Direct substitution verifies the resulting |S> is annihilated by every Q_a, so the kernel has dimension one. Expand Omega=sum_nm |n><m| tensor C_nm. Rank-one support gives C_nm=P C_nm P=c_nm P. Hence Omega=sigma_A tensor P. Positivity and unit trace pass to sigma_A; partial trace gives uniqueness.')
p('For address observable B and color observable C, expectations therefore factor as Tr(sigma_A B) times &lt;S|C|S&gt;. Address-controlled collective transformations U_n tensor U_n tensor U_n with U_n in SU(3) leave |S> fixed and cannot encode different address labels into this sector. A prospective decoder that deletes address labels cannot reconstruct them from this fixed color state. Exact support is stronger than zero mean charge; omitted gluon, flavor or spatial factors can change the applicable representation. Spin, confinement, binding, a particle spectrum and arithmetic selection of SU(3) remain open.')
h('4. Consequence for a particle/component interface')
p('The replay and the color theorem answer complementary questions about the same frozen implementation. Changing the assembly order changes its component-number distribution while preserving integer conservation. The color routine cannot resolve that ambiguity: its function reads no assembly output, and its unique exact singlet carries no independently variable color-state label. Thus the results locate where a later address-to-particle decoder must retain information. They do not establish that such a decoder has already been physically completed.')
p('For example, take two distinct address preparations |a><a| and |b><b|, each tensored with |S><S|. Their address registers are distinguishable, but both reduced color states equal |S><S|. For any color measurement effect E, both give probability <S|E|S>. Deleting the address register therefore makes the preparations indistinguishable by color-only queries. Address-controlled collective SU(3) rotations cannot repair this loss. This example applies the proven restriction to interface design.')
p('A fixed ascending or descending assembly is a valid declared algorithm. The measured TV is a counterexample to equality of the two tested aggregate component distributions; zero TV would not by itself prove equality of per-address outputs or invariance under every possible order. The present calculation therefore rejects only the stronger order-independent interpretation for which this nonzero counterexample is sufficient.')
p('For maintainers extending the Stage-3 decoder, the concrete workflow is: declare which address/component variables the extension reads; retain that register when outputs depend on its labels; rerun integer reconstruction and conditional component comparisons for the declared prime order; and test all eight total generators plus symmetry-breaking controls for any changed color state. The supplied color routine remains an adopted consistency contract until an explicit address-dependent coupling is calculated. This is guidance for using the supplied replay and tests, not a newly implemented coupling or release tool. A larger state space or additional factors may change the information constraint, but no such extension is implemented or claimed here. Reproducing established identities remains a valid consistency result; the new source-specific knowledge is which outputs are actually connected and where the proposed explanatory connection remains open.')
page()
